  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.93,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings flatten out at about 1.0 from 7 h on, which is what a plate reader does when it saturates. To check, I diluted the 18 h aliquot. At 10x it read 0.3934 and 0.3961 (×10 = about 3.95). At 40x it read 0.1012 and 0.0943 (×40 = about 3.91). Two dilutions 4-fold apart give the same back-calculated OD, so the diluted reads are in the reader's proportional range. Both are about 4x the undiluted reading of 0.99. The 12 h aliquot at 10x read 0.4026 and 0.4178 (×10 = about 4.1), so the true biomass was already near 4 well into the flat stretch. The real plateau is around OD 3.9–4.1, not 1.0. Over the final hours the biomass is about 4 times higher than the undiluted readings show. Best estimate at 18 h: OD ≈ 3.93 (mean of the two dilution levels)."
  },
